SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Russia's Putin authorises 'special military operation' against Ukraine","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-02-24","url":"https://m.investing.com/news/world-news/russias-putin-authorises-special-military-operation-against-ukraine-2770751?ampMode=1","claim":"Putin said the operation's goal was to protect people in Donbas and to demilitarise and denazify Ukraine, making the war's core aim explicit.","locator":"Reuters lead paragraph / quoted address in search result snippet","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous Reuters reporting on Putin's own televised announcement; direct quote and immediate publication date match the target period.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target period and program origin point.","ruler_attribution":"Direct and strong; this is Putin's own public statement, though self-justifying and contested by Ukraine and Western governments.","contrary_evidence":["Ukraine and Western officials characterized the invasion as an imperialist war, not a protective operation."],"lenses":["8B.1","8B.2","8B.3"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Russia reframes war goals as Ukrainians advance near Kyiv","publisher":"Euronews (Reuters)","publication_date":"2022-03-26","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/03/26/uk-ukraine-crisis","claim":"Moscow signalled it was scaling back its ambitions in Ukraine to focus on Donbass, saying the first phase was mostly complete and that the main goal was the 'liberation of Donbass'.","locator":"lines 615-620","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting with a precise date and a concrete statement by the Russian defence ministry during the 2022 campaign.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022 and squarely about execution of the war program.","ruler_attribution":"Strong but indirect; the statement came from the Russian defence ministry under Putin's rule and was used to justify a course correction after setbacks.","contrary_evidence":["The same report says Russian troops had failed to capture any major city in the first month and were being pushed back near Kyiv."],"lenses":["8B.8","8B.9","8B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Russia says it will sharply cut military activity near Kyiv, Chernihiv","publisher":"Reuters via Yahoo News","publication_date":"2022-03-29","url":"https://www.yahoo.com/news/russia-says-drastically-cut-military-122350725.html","claim":"Russia said it would sharply reduce military activity around Kyiv and Chernihiv to increase mutual trust and create conditions for further negotiations.","locator":"Reuters lede / search snippet","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters report on a specific operational pause announced after Istanbul talks; the claim is temporally and causally well anchored.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Within the target year and directly about tactical adaptation in the war.","ruler_attribution":"Strongly attributable to Putin's war leadership, though the announcement was made by the Russian military delegation rather than Putin personally.","contrary_evidence":["The reduction did not cover Russian offensives elsewhere and was widely read as a repositioning after setbacks."],"lenses":["8B.8","8B.9"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Instructions following a meeting on socioeconomic support for regions","publisher":"President of Russia","publication_date":"2022-04-10","url":"https://en.kremlin.ru/acts/assignments/orders/copy/68175","claim":"Putin approved instructions to expand support for families that lost income or jobs after March 1, 2022, increase pensions, social benefits, wages, minimum wage and subsistence minimum, fund regional budgets and infrastructure, and bring down poverty and income inequality.","locator":"official instructions summary / search snippet","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official presidential instructions with concrete deadlines, fiscal channels, and implementation tasks.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022 and tightly tied to wartime domestic management.","ruler_attribution":"Direct; the instructions were approved by Putin and delegated to government bodies for implementation.","contrary_evidence":["This is a directive package, not proof that all intended measures were fully delivered on time."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.6","8B.8"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Russia calls up 300,000 reservists, says 6,000 soldiers killed in Ukraine","publisher":"Euronews (Reuters)","publication_date":"2022-09-22","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/09/22/ukraine-crisis-putin-mobilisation","claim":"Putin ordered Russia's first mobilisation since World War Two after a major battlefield reversal, with Shoigu saying 300,000 reservists would be drafted to support the war in Ukraine.","locator":"lines 656-673","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting on a major 2022 strategic decision and its immediate implementation parameters.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the target year and a central adaptation point.","ruler_attribution":"Strong; the mobilisation followed Putin's order and was part of the state response to battlefield reversals under his command.","contrary_evidence":["The same story reports heavy casualties and frames the mobilisation as a response to setbacks rather than evidence of prior success."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.3","8B.5","8B.9"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Russia excludes some IT professionals, bankers and journalists from mobilisation","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-09-23","url":"https://uk.investing.com/news/world-news/russia-excludes-some-it-professionals-bankers-and-state-journalists-from-mobilisation-2759912","claim":"Russia exempted some bankers, IT workers and journalists from mobilisation in order to keep critical industries and the financial system functioning smoothly.","locator":"lines 424-443","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reports an explicit policy exception with stated operational rationale from the central bank and defence ministry.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the target year and part of wartime implementation.","ruler_attribution":"Strongly attributable to Putin's governing network, though the measure is implemented by ministries and the central bank rather than Putin personally.","contrary_evidence":["The exemptions also reveal that mobilisation was causing practical strain and required improvisation."],"lenses":["8B.4","8B.5","8B.8"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Russia names air force general to lead its forces in Ukraine","publisher":"Euronews (Reuters)","publication_date":"2022-10-09","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/10/09/ukraine-crisis-russia-military","claim":"Russia's Defence Ministry named Sergei Surovikin overall commander of forces fighting in Ukraine after a series of dramatic reverses, as part of an effort to centralise command and control.","locator":"lines 659-669","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters coverage of a major command reshuffle with explicit mention of the operational rationale.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022 and clearly part of wartime adaptation.","ruler_attribution":"Strong; the command change occurred under Putin's war leadership, though the ministerial chain executed it.","contrary_evidence":["Command changes can indicate failure as well as adaptation; the appointment does not itself prove improved battlefield performance."],"lenses":["8B.4","8B.5","8B.8"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Russia says it has completed retreat from Kherson","publisher":"ThePrint (Reuters)","publication_date":"2022-11-11","url":"https://theprint.in/world/russia-says-it-has-completed-retreat-from-kherson/1211267/","claim":"Russia said it had completed its withdrawal from Kherson, a lightning-fast retreat of tens of thousands of troops that Reuters described as a major setback and the loss of the only regional capital Russia captured after the invasion.","locator":"lines 123-153","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters report with clear attribution and detailed battlefield consequences; the article provides a strong negative outcome marker for the war program.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022 and decisive for end-of-year war performance.","ruler_attribution":"Strong; the withdrawal was ordered by Russia's defence ministry under Putin's overall war authority, though Surovikin and Shoigu handled the immediate decision.","contrary_evidence":["Russian officials framed the move as an orderly transfer to defensive lines and said they were still committed to the operation's goals."],"lenses":["8B.7","8B.9","8B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Putin tells Russian defence industry to up its game for Ukraine war","publisher":"Euronews (Reuters)","publication_date":"2022-12-24","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/12/24/ukraine-crisis-putin-arms","claim":"Putin told defence-industry chiefs that the key task was to provide frontline units with weapons, equipment, ammunition and gear in the necessary quantities and shortest timeframes.","locator":"Reuters lede / search result snippet","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters published this as a concrete wartime directive from Putin to the industrial base.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022 and tied to execution of the war program.","ruler_attribution":"Direct; this is Putin personally tasking the industrial base under wartime conditions.","contrary_evidence":["The article is an exhortation, not proof that the required quantities were actually delivered on schedule."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.4","8B.6"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Instructions on developing unmanned aircraft systems","publisher":"President of Russia","publication_date":"2022-12-30","url":"https://en.kremlin.ru/acts/assignments/orders/copy/70312","claim":"Putin ordered creation of a government commission, a national strategy to 2030 and 2035, procurement plans, certification rules, specialist training, and airspace integration for unmanned aircraft systems.","locator":"official instructions summary / search snippet","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official presidential instructions with a detailed implementation architecture, timelines, and institutional owners.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022, showing late-year institutionalisation of a war-and-industrial priority.","ruler_attribution":"Direct; the instructions were Putin's and assigned to government, ministries, security agencies, and the central bank for follow-through.","contrary_evidence":["This is a planning and institution-building directive; 2022 alone does not show how fully the system executed it."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.4","8B.6","8B.8"]}

**Search and Rejection Summary**
- I considered roughly 30 documents across official Kremlin transcripts, Reuters/Euronews stories, World Bank and IMF material, Defence Department analysis, and a few later retrospective pieces.
- Kept the sources that most directly traced Putin's 2022 program from declaration to action and outcome: invasion goals, tactical retreats/reframing, mobilisation, personnel changes, industrial tasking, and battlefield reverses.
- Rejected as duplicates or low-yield:
- Multiple later 2023-2025 recaps on Gerasimov, Surovikin, and war performance that repeated the same battlefield narrative without adding 2022-specific execution evidence.
- Broad Russia country indicators and governance metrics already present in local priors, because they are context rather than ruler-specific effectiveness evidence.
- General corruption, repression, and casualty articles that did not illuminate program-to-action-to-outcome causality for 8B.
- Blocked or impractical Kremlin page opens that timed out; where the direct source was still useful, I relied on the search snippet or search-result summary rather than inventing a citation.
- Out-of-period follow-ups were excluded unless they were only being used to describe a 2022 event already within the target period.

**Remaining Gaps**
- Direct 2022 internal performance data from the Russian military, procurement system, and industrial ministries remain thin. The dossier shows mobilisation and adaptation, but not full delivery metrics.
- Attribution is strong for Putin's broad program, weaker for some specific command and procurement moves that were executed by Shoigu, Gerasimov, Surovikin, or ministries on his behalf.
- I did not find a clean, independent 2022 audit of whether the late-2022 defence-industrial and UAV directives actually translated into sustained battlefield advantage before year-end.
- If you want tighter separation between "frantic adaptation" and "genuinely effective execution," the best next sources would be Russian-language budget/execution records, defence-industrial procurement data, or serious academic histories of the 2022 campaign.
